.TH COINBASE\-MCP\-SERVER 1 "2026-09-08" "1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coinbase\-mcp\-server \- MCP server for the Coinbase Advanced Trade API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coinbase-mcp-server
[\fB\-\-stdio\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B coinbase-mcp-server
is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets AI assistants interact
with the Coinbase Advanced Trade API: account balances, order placement,
portfolio and product data, technical indicators, chart-pattern and
sentiment analysis, and market-event tools.
.PP
.B WARNING:
when configured with live API keys this software can place real trades
and move real funds on your Coinbase account. Use read-only or sandbox
keys during evaluation, and dry-run mode before trading with real money.
.PP
By default the server starts in HTTP mode and listens on the port given
by \fBPORT\fR (3000 if unset). Pass \fB\-\-stdio\fR to use stdin/stdout
transport for direct embedding in desktop MCP hosts such as Claude Code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-stdio
Use stdio transport. The MCP host communicates over stdin/stdout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COINBASE_API_KEY_NAME
Coinbase Advanced Trade API key name, e.g.
\fIorganizations/<org>/apiKeys/<key>\fR. Required.
.TP
.B COINBASE_PRIVATE_KEY
PEM-encoded EC private key matching the API key name. Required.
.TP
.B PORT
TCP port for HTTP mode. Defaults to 3000. Ignored with \fB\-\-stdio\fR.
.SH FILES
.B /usr/lib/coinbase-mcp-server
Installed application code and vendored Node.js dependencies.
.SH SEE ALSO
Coinbase Advanced Trade API documentation:
.UR https://docs.cdp.coinbase.com/advanced-trade/
.UE
